  "sections": {
    "work": [
      {
        "kind": "quote",
        "text": "Landscapes should be represented so that the trees may be half in light and half in shadow; but it is better to do them when the sun is covered with clouds, for then the trees are lighted by the general light of the sky, and the general darkness of the earth.",
        "lead": "Leonardo's later advice on drawing a landscape:",
        "source": {
          "author": "Leonardo da Vinci",
          "title": "The Notebooks of Leonardo da Vinci",
          "readAt": "https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/5000/pg5000.txt",
          "accessed": "2026-11-03",
          "tier": 1,
          "publisher": "Translated by Jean Paul Richter",
          "year": "1888",
          "license": "Public domain"
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "quote",
        "text": "His earliest dated drawing is a Landscape of the Arno Valley, 1473, which shows the river, the mountains, Montelupo Castle and the farmlands beyond it in great detail.",
        "source": {
